From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BerryMC <148406068+BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:42:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix four correctness issues found in patch audit

1. crop.optimize-growth was dead config - BlockCrops/BlockStem always
   used the nextFloat() path regardless of the toggle. Now the vanilla
   nextInt(bound) path is restored when the option is off (its default).
   Probability equivalence verified empirically over 10 bounds.

2. hopper.optimize scanned only the hopper's own chunk while
   World#getEntities scans the AABB-expanded chunk block. A candidate in
   a neighbouring chunk at a border would have been skipped. Now the
   check only skips when the expanded AABB stays within a single loaded
   chunk, and every slice the vanilla scan touches is verified empty.

3. async-json-list-save flushed pending writes at the START of
   MinecraftServer#stop, before savePlayers/saveChunks could submit more.
   Moved the flush to the very end of shutdown. Also broadened the
   executor's catch to Throwable so write failures are never silent.

4. Ban-list date parsing regressed for textual zone ids: the old
   SimpleDateFormat accepted 'UTC'/'GMT' while the strict
   DateTimeFormatter threw, silently losing the date. Added a
   zone-or-offset fallback formatter (verified all four sample formats
   now parse identically to the old implementation).

Also hardened the configs/ migration: cross-device moves now fall back
to copy+delete instead of aborting startup.

